 "rules": "Ranked-choice voting is used for the general election. If no candidate wins a majority of first choices, the Secretary of State runs a central RCV tabulation in Augusta after collecting ballots from municipalities, which has taken about a week in past RCV races. With only two candidates on the ballot (Collins, Jackson), the first-round count normally decides the race; RCV would only matter through write-ins. Maine has not replaced a party nominee in any prior election; Jackson was nominated by a party convention after the primary winner withdrew.",
